@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam componentBorderColor #40546A
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EAF2FC
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #E3F1D3
skinparam databaseBorderColor #40546A
skinparam ArrowColor #526579
skinparam ArrowFontSize 14
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam titleFontSize 24
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam legendBorderColor #CBD5E1

title PolyNTU architecture\nFunctional modules

component "Participant browser\nReact interface" as Browser
component "Market service\nquotes, trades, pricing,\nmarket lifecycle\n\nparallel: requests are tasks on\nthe Tokio multi-thread runtime,\nwhich runs one worker thread\nper core" as Service
component "Settlement worker\nbracket scheduling, resolution,\nclaim settlement\n\nparallel: up to 8 independent\nmarkets settle at once\n(instance row lock keeps each\nmarket internally serial)" as Worker
database "PostgreSQL\naccounts, markets, trades,\nevidence, ledger\n\nparallel: 32-connection pool,\nrow locks order writes" as Db
component "External data sources\nconfigured resolvers and\nthe NTU bus feed" as Sources

Browser --> Service : trade, publish, resolve
Service --> Browser : live updates
Service --> Db : reads and writes
Worker --> Db : closes, resolves, settles
Worker --> Sources : fetches the outcome

legend bottom left
  One Rust process serves the browser and runs the settlement worker;
  both read and write the same database.
  The process runs Tokio's multi-thread runtime: HTTP requests, the worker,
  the event listener, and the clock refresher run as separate tasks, so
  independent work uses multiple cores. Work inside one market stays serial
  under its row lock.
endlegend
@enduml
